    <item>
      <title>Rich Content</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/rich-content/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 10 Mar 2019 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/rich-content/</guid>
      <description>A brief description of Hugo Shortcodes</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Hugo ships with several <a href="https://gohugo.io/content-management/shortcodes/#use-hugos-built-in-shortcodes">Built-in Shortcodes</a> for rich content, along with a <a href="https://gohugo.io/about/hugo-and-gdpr/">Privacy Config</a> and a set of Simple Shortcodes that enable static and no-JS versions of various social media embeds.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="images">Images</h2>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Cheat sheet for this site.</strong> Image lookup and processing live in
<code>layouts/_default/_markup/render-image.html</code>, <code>layouts/shortcodes/img.html</code>
and <code>layouts/partials/image/</code>. The full option list is in the comment at the
top of <code>layouts/shortcodes/img.html</code>.</p></blockquote>
<h3 id="where-to-put-images">Where to put images</h3>
<p>Put shared images in <strong><code>assets/images/</code></strong>. Images there can be cropped and resized at build time.
Any of these path styles works, from any post:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"><code class="language-markdown" data-lang="markdown"><span class="line"><span class="cl">![<span class="nt">alt</span>](<span class="na">fig.png</span>)
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">![<span class="nt">alt</span>](<span class="na">images/fig.png</span>)
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">![<span class="nt">alt</span>](<span class="na">/images/fig.png</span>)
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">![<span class="nt">alt</span>](<span class="na">../images/fig.png</span>)
</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Lookup order:</p>
<ol>
<li>the post&rsquo;s own folder (when the post is a folder with an <code>index.md</code>)</li>
<li>the section folder, e.g. <code>content/posts/images/</code></li>
<li><code>assets/</code> and <code>assets/images/</code></li>
<li><code>static/</code> and <code>static/images/</code> (served as-is, <strong>cannot</strong> be cropped or resized; only the CSS display options work)</li>
</ol>
<p>If an image isn&rsquo;t found, <code>hugo</code> prints a <code>WARN Image &quot;...&quot; not found</code> line. Check the build output.</p>
<p>Third-party images work as usual:</p>
<p><img loading="lazy" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1662141978148-2eeb2afb3837?ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;ixid=MnwxMjA3fDB8MHxwaG90by1wYWdlfHx8fGVufDB8fHx8&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=772&amp;q=80" alt="" /></p>
<h3 id="quick-crop-in-plain-markdown">Quick crop in plain markdown</h3>
<p>Add options after a <code>?</code>:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"><code class="language-markdown" data-lang="markdown"><span class="line"><span class="cl">![<span class="nt">Attractor</span>](<span class="na">images/CLV1_in_XZfor_truth.png?fill=600x300&amp;anchor=top</span>)
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">![<span class="nt">Small plot</span>](<span class="na">images/4dvar-4dvarnet-plot.png?resize=400x</span>)
</span></span></code></pre></div><p><img loading="lazy" src="/images/CLV1_in_XZfor_truth_hu_6181e50350fc410a.png" alt="Attractor" /></p>
<h3 id="full-control-the-img-shortcode">Full control: the <code>img</code> shortcode</h3>
<div class="highlight"><pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"><code class="language-markdown" data-lang="markdown"><span class="line"><span class="cl">{{<span class="p">&lt;</span> <span class="nt">img</span> <span class="na">src</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;images/CLV1_in_XZfor_truth.png&#34;</span> <span class="na">fill</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;800x400&#34;</span> <span class="na">anchor</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;top&#34;</span>
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">        <span class="na">width</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;70%&#34;</span> <span class="na">align</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;center&#34;</span> <span class="na">caption</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;Covariant Lyapunov vector 1&#34;</span> <span class="na">link</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;true&#34;</span> <span class="p">&gt;</span>}}
</span></span></code></pre></div><figure class="img-sc img-center"><a href="/images/CLV1_in_XZfor_truth.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img loading="lazy" src="/images/CLV1_in_XZfor_truth_hu_8093c4e955f4354a.png" alt="Covariant Lyapunov vector 1" width="800" height="400" style="width:70%" /></a><figcaption><p>Covariant Lyapunov vector 1</p></figcaption>
</figure>

<p><strong>Cropping and resizing</strong> (makes a new image file at build time; for images in <code>assets/</code> or a post&rsquo;s own folder; pick one):</p>
<table>
  <thead>
      <tr>
          <th>Option</th>
          <th>Example</th>
          <th>What it does</th>
      </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
      <tr>
          <td><code>fill</code></td>
          <td><code>fill=&quot;800x400&quot;</code></td>
          <td>scale <strong>and</strong> crop to exactly 800×400 (usually what you want)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td><code>crop</code></td>
          <td><code>crop=&quot;800x400&quot;</code></td>
          <td>cut an 800×400 region out of the original, no scaling</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td><code>fit</code></td>
          <td><code>fit=&quot;800x400&quot;</code></td>
          <td>shrink to fit inside 800×400, keep the aspect ratio</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td><code>resize</code></td>
          <td><code>resize=&quot;600x&quot;</code>, <code>resize=&quot;x400&quot;</code></td>
          <td>scale to a width and/or height</td>
      </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Order of precedence if several are given: <code>fill</code> &gt; <code>crop</code> &gt; <code>fit</code> &gt; <code>resize</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Modifiers:</strong></p>
<table>
  <thead>
      <tr>
          <th>Option</th>
          <th>Values</th>
          <th>Notes</th>
      </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
      <tr>
          <td><code>anchor</code></td>
          <td><code>center</code> (default), <code>smart</code>, <code>top</code>, <code>bottom</code>, <code>left</code>, <code>right</code>, <code>topleft</code>, <code>topright</code>, <code>bottomleft</code>, <code>bottomright</code></td>
          <td>which part survives a <code>fill</code>/<code>crop</code>; <code>smart</code> lets Hugo pick the most detailed area</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td><code>quality</code></td>
          <td><code>1</code>–<code>100</code></td>
          <td>JPEG/WebP quality</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td><code>rotate</code></td>
          <td><code>90</code>, <code>180</code>, <code>270</code></td>
          <td>counter-clockwise rotation</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td><code>format</code></td>
          <td><code>webp</code>, <code>png</code>, <code>jpg</code></td>
          <td>convert the output</td>
      </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Display only</strong> (CSS, original file untouched; also works for SVGs and <code>static/</code> images):</p>
<table>
  <thead>
      <tr>
          <th>Option</th>
          <th>Example</th>
          <th>What it does</th>
      </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
      <tr>
          <td><code>width</code> / <code>height</code></td>
          <td><code>width=&quot;70%&quot;</code>, <code>width=&quot;400px&quot;</code></td>
          <td>size on the page</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td><code>ratio</code></td>
          <td><code>ratio=&quot;16/9&quot;</code>, <code>ratio=&quot;1/1&quot;</code></td>
          <td>crop the visible area to this aspect ratio</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td><code>position</code></td>
          <td><code>position=&quot;30% 20%&quot;</code></td>
          <td>with <code>ratio</code>: the focus point (x% y%) that stays in view. Use this for a precise crop that <code>anchor</code> can&rsquo;t express</td>
      </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Other:</strong> <code>alt</code>, <code>caption</code> (markdown allowed), <code>title</code>, <code>align</code> (<code>left</code>, <code>center</code>, <code>right</code>), <code>link</code> (<code>&quot;true&quot;</code> opens the original on click, or give a URL), <code>class</code>.</p>
<h3 id="recipes">Recipes</h3>
<div class="highlight"><pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"><code class="language-markdown" data-lang="markdown"><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="c">&lt;!-- Square thumbnail from the top-left corner --&gt;</span>
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">{{<span class="p">&lt;</span> <span class="nt">img</span> <span class="na">src</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;images/enhanced_L63_attr_12.png&#34;</span> <span class="na">fill</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;400x400&#34;</span> <span class="na">anchor</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;topleft&#34;</span> <span class="p">&gt;</span>}}
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="c">&lt;!-- Shrink a huge figure so the page loads fast, keep full-res on click --&gt;</span>
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">{{<span class="p">&lt;</span> <span class="nt">img</span> <span class="na">src</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;images/enhanced_L63_attr_12.png&#34;</span> <span class="na">resize</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;1200x&#34;</span> <span class="na">link</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;true&#34;</span> <span class="p">&gt;</span>}}
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="c">&lt;!-- Banner crop with an exact focus point (CSS) --&gt;</span>
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">{{<span class="p">&lt;</span> <span class="nt">img</span> <span class="na">src</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;images/CLV2_in_XZfor_truth.png&#34;</span> <span class="na">resize</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;1500x&#34;</span> <span class="na">ratio</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;21/9&#34;</span> <span class="na">position</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;50% 30%&#34;</span> <span class="p">&gt;</span>}}
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="c">&lt;!-- Small right-aligned image with a caption --&gt;</span>
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">{{<span class="p">&lt;</span> <span class="nt">img</span> <span class="na">src</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;images/schematic.png&#34;</span> <span class="na">fit</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;300x300&#34;</span> <span class="na">align</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;right&#34;</span> <span class="na">caption</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">&#34;*Schematic*&#34;</span> <span class="p">&gt;</span>}}
</span></span></code></pre></div><figure class="img-sc"><img loading="lazy" src="/images/enhanced_L63_attr_12_hu_31870c4479e3f0cd.png" alt="fill 400x400, anchor topleft" width="400" height="400" /><figcaption><p>fill 400x400, anchor topleft</p></figcaption>
</figure>

<figure class="img-sc"><img loading="lazy" src="/images/CLV2_in_XZfor_truth_hu_23d34c621db35b99.png" alt="ratio 21/9, position 50% 30%" width="1500" height="1000" style="aspect-ratio:21/9;object-fit:cover;width:100%;object-position:50% 30%" /><figcaption><p>ratio 21/9, position 50% 30%</p></figcaption>
</figure>

